            <ArticleTitle>Medial thigh pain: neurology or urology?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>799</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Flank pain, irritative urinary symptoms, and hematuria are traditional symptoms of urolithiasis. We report a case of urolithiasis in a neobladder in a patient with a chief complaint of medial thigh pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
